  "correct": "3",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nPrincipal (P) = Rs. 40,000\n\nTime (T) = 4 years\n\nSimple Interest (SI) = Rs. 24,000\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nSI = (P × R × T) ÷ 100\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ 24,000 = (40,000 × R × 4) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ 24,000 = (1,60,000 × R) ÷ 100\n\n⇒ 24,000 × 100 = 1,60,000 × R\n\n⇒ 24,00,000 = 1,60,000 × R\n\n⇒ R = 24,00,000 ÷ 1,60,000\n\n⇒ R = 15\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 15%.**",
